cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use INDUS-DEDUCT code, benchmark data, or restoration catalog, please cite this work."
title: "INDUS-DEDUCT: A Calibrated, Anti-Hallucination Computational Benchmark for the Indus Valley Script"
version: "1.0.0-preprint"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Emre & Emare INDUS-DEDUCT Research Collective"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - indus-script
  - harappan
  - computational-epigraphy
  - undeciphered-scripts
  - paleo-linguistics
  - benchmark
  - reproducible-research
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end 13-layer calibrated computational epigraphy benchmark across 5,679 Indus Valley
  inscriptions, featuring five-way known-answer and non-linguistic calibration (Ur III Sumerian,
  Linear B, Linear A, Non-Linguistic Stamps), exact 23-seal Max-CSP identifiability boundaries,
  Mohenjo-daro Copper Tablet internal Rosetta analysis, 700-year de-confounded paleographic drift
  chains, and a 690-inscription strict Leave-One-City-Out damaged restoration catalog.
